{
  "name": "Understanding the Timeline for Backsplash Tile Installation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When you're eager for a new kitchen backsplash, knowing what to expect timeline-wise can really help manage your project. Here's a breakdown of the typical phases:",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "**Phase 1: Preparation & Planning**",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "This is where you clear your counters, protect surfaces, and get the wall ready. If there's an old backsplash, demo happens here. We'll also shut off nearby power and remove cover plates. This stage is crucial for a smooth installation and usually takes a few hours to a half-day, depending on the scope.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4",
      "text": "**Phase 2: Tile Setting**",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5",
      "text": "After wall prep, we'll lay out the tile and start setting it with mortar. This is where the magic happens, but patience is key! The mortar needs about 24 hours to properly dry and set the tiles securely. Don't rush this step, or your tiles might shift.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 6",
      "text": "**Phase 3: Grouting**",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 7",
      "text": "Once the mortar is dry, it's time for grouting. This fills the spaces between your tiles, sealing them and making your backsplash look finished. Grout needs time to cure, which can be anywhere from 24 hours to three days, depending on the product used. We make sure to use the right flexible caulk for the joint where the backsplash meets the countertop, rather than grout, to allow for movement and prevent cracking.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 7
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 8",
      "text": "**Phase 4: Finishing Touches**",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 8
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 9",
      "text": "This final stage involves sealing the grout (if necessary, depending on the type), reinstalling outlet covers, and moving appliances back into place. Your kitchen will be ready to show off!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 9
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 10",
      "text": "HH Remodeling LLC handles all these phases with expertise, ensuring a beautiful and durable result for your kitchen in Aurora, Colorado Springs, or any of the surrounding Denver areas. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 10
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
